## Candidate synthesis

Generate 2–5 materially different immutable candidate drafts. Vary the source of discrimination: intervention/randomized contrast; blocked/factorial screening; matching/counterbalancing; calibration/orthogonal measurement; positive/negative controls; justified natural/quasi experiment; valid sequential/adaptive design; measurement-first pilot; computational benchmark. If only one credible design exists, emit that single draft and set `only_credible_explanation` to a non-empty account of why each materially different alternative cannot answer the question; otherwise set it to null.

Every draft carries a unique, non-empty, stable `candidate_id`. This stage proposes; it does not gate, rank or select. Do not emit a selected design, gate verdict, typed stop or outcome.

Each draft emits:

- unique stable `candidate_id` and semantic `credibility_assessment` (`credible` or `infeasible`), design family, rationale and estimand;
- units/sampling frame/factors/treatments/comparator/allocation, including justified omissions;
- a hypothesis × possible-observation matrix;
- an auxiliary-failure × possible-observation matrix for calibration error, leakage, confounding, model misspecification and domain shift;
- measurement model (construct mapping, instruments, calibration, uncertainty, scope/transportability, positive/negative/orthogonal controls, auxiliary ledger); when validity or transportability is uncertain, include a bounded calibration sub-experiment with trigger, acceptance criterion, budget/`max_runs`, and failure disposition;
- identification contrast, causal model when applicable, assumptions and non-identifiable remainder;
- information justification (power/MDE, confidence-width, equivalence margin, simulation, sensitivity or another sourced method);
- preregistered analysis, exclusions, missing data, multiplicity, robustness/sensitivity and confirmatory/exploratory boundary;
- stopping/adaptation/interim/error-control and positive `max_runs`;
- executor binding with exact input/output/report contract and typed failures;
- ethics/safety, reproducibility package and limitations;
- flat semantic ED-1 inputs: `ethics_safety`, `feasibility`, `rivals_differ`, `equivalence_prespecified`, `identification`, `measurement_validity`, `information_adequacy`, `bias_control`, `preregistration`, `reproducibility`, each with a short evidence basis.

A draft is immutable after this response. The caller checks ID uniqueness and cardinality in ED-C, computes each ED-1 result in `lisp_eval`, and passes the exact drafts plus receipts to `select-design`; never regenerate or revise a candidate after observing its gate result.

Return JSON only with exactly `candidate_drafts`, `only_credible_explanation`.
